# Backend

- The backend is Go. The frontend stays TypeScript and React.
- Serve HTTP with the Go standard library. Add a web framework only after a later rule chooses one.
- Handle requests in parallel. Keep CPU and memory use low.
- SQLite accepts one write at a time. Reads and requests that are not writing continue in parallel.
- A failure inside one request stays inside that request. The process keeps serving.
- The SQLite driver, ports, and resource numbers are not decided yet. Wait for a later rule before choosing them.
